    "agent_last_message": "Implemented the Rust CLI as a standard Cargo project under [output/Cargo.toml](/workspace/output/Cargo.toml:1) and [output/src/main.rs](/workspace/output/src/main.rs:1). The manifest keeps `[dependencies]` empty, the binary accepts `--input` and `--output`, validates arguments strictly, writes the required JSON shape, returns `1` for invalid invocation/input errors, and returns `2` on unexpected panic via `catch_unwind`.\n\nThe analyzer is buffered and streaming rather than whole-file, so memory stays bounded for large files. It counts bytes as characters, counts lines exactly per the spec, splits words only on the six specified ASCII whitespace bytes, lowercases words for frequency counting, sorts `top_words` by descending count then ascending lexicographic order, and rejects malformed UTF-8 input as exit code `1`.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo build --release --manifest-path /workspace/output/Cargo.toml`\n- `cargo test --manifest-path /workspace/output/Cargo.toml`\n- End-to-end `cargo run --release --manifest-path /workspace/output/Cargo.toml -- ...` checks for empty/newline/no-trailing-newline/tie-ordering/invalid-UTF-8 cases all matched the spec\n\n`rustfmt` is not installed in this environment, so I could not run `cargo fmt`.",
